children.push(P("Mechanism B splits sharply by method: DBSCAN recovers it far better than blind K-Means (0.72 vs. 0.06), while Spectral Clustering does not (0.02, indistinguishable from K-Means). Mechanism C remains at or near chance for all three methods (≤ 0.007), reinforcing it as invisible to every generic method tested here, not only K-Means. Mechanism A — already well recovered by the nonlinear front ends earlier in this section — is not particularly well recovered by any of the three blind clustering-step swaps on the linear PCA front end (0.11, 0.08, 0.00), consistent with the front end, rather than the clustering step, being what matters for mechanism A."));
children.push(P("To check whether DBSCAN’s advantage on mechanism B is a general property of DBSCAN or specific to that mechanism’s geometry, we ran the identical grid-searched three-method comparison on the three real datasets already used for the Section 4.2 check (Wine, Breast Cancer, Digits)."));
